{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "007L", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-algebraic-structures}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f07d3de0b61f53b1209953a26da90e8fdd68cc785ad1061432a073648eb46e73", "source_text": "Algebraic structures", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d6a80f01eb77786cc3719c8f1265271cda0186aeacb4cf519e18de4d1b474414", "unit_id": "tag:007L:title"}
{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "007L", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e011f372e9a07dbfe6148949b5e79d8ed05c5cb0b8d17552c15e5938ed6f2bc5", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn this section we mildly formalize the notions we have\nencountered in the sections above.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:288b0fd2adae9d39f01483bad5df59d22c3a11cf2ff3de077c67df9fded97d75", "unit_id": "tag:007L:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "007L", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$F : \\mathcal{C} \\to \\textit{Sets}$", "MATH_0003": "$F$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0005": "$F$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0007": "$F$", "MATH_0008": "$F$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\item", "STRUCT_0006": "\\end{enumerate}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-algebraic-structure}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9b99b92cf9efcba8d10d3432977fab4e9a3ae0e3698d1808c391acf5b6eb261c", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:7427cfd332a34fc1bfd14b1b3f3d64904db9c74c79c3a97ebb1452c8391e4cbc", "source_text": "A <TEXTITOPEN_0001>type of algebraic structure<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> is given by a category <MATH_0001>\nand a functor <MATH_0002> with the\nfollowing properties\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0003> is faithful,\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0004> has limits and <MATH_0005> commutes with limits,\n<STRUCT_0004> <MATH_0006> has filtered colimits and <MATH_0007> commutes with them, and\n<STRUCT_0005> <MATH_0008> reflects isomorphisms.\n<STRUCT_0006>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:03cbdcf4da708eb4bffdec2b561144b337a3b071b4f68b5782bac578700bf562", "unit_id": "tag:007M:statement"}
{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "007L", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{categories-remark-big-categories}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:35663afde59d1e6edb66b77e3bb05f2a94c54918ec53a511f854fa5c9a9c1d9f", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nWe make this definition to point out the properties\nwe will use in a number of arguments below.  But we will\nnot actually study this notion in any great detail, since we\nare prohibited from studying ``big'' categories by convention,\nexcept for those listed in\nCategories, Remark <REF_0001>.\nAmong those the following have the required properties.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:9122df6375bc265b6837f67d7959ad6d2e1362af1c068319d4d074417230bbff", "unit_id": "tag:007L:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "007L", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$R$", "MATH_0002": "$R$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\item", "STRUCT_0006": "\\item", "STRUCT_0007": "\\item", "STRUCT_0008": "\\item", "STRUCT_0009": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-list-algebraic-structures}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:103c4d2b7eba8315df9a978e976ac0b41d8778b6af7fbee40f280209877d12d3", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3616a5dc6a2b6ccae247ecdc3975a696ec213aefc654dc1aedc470e1ee8a51c2", "source_text": "The following categories, endowed with the obvious forgetful\nfunctor, define types of algebraic structures:\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> The category of pointed sets.\n<STRUCT_0003> The category of abelian groups.\n<STRUCT_0004> The category of groups.\n<STRUCT_0005> The category of monoids.\n<STRUCT_0006> The category of rings.\n<STRUCT_0007> The category of <MATH_0001>-modules for a fixed ring <MATH_0002>.\n<STRUCT_0008> The category of Lie algebras over a fixed field.\n<STRUCT_0009>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:326a28dae02c147014730056d5dcc8d6cba3a499f52e299b155c00de89ad0b68", "unit_id": "tag:007N:statement"}
